    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e11df6f_c0a28678",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-02T20:31:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have been interpreting \"pe\" to mean the state object of the policy engine, but evidently this object can be described as just the state pertaining to discovery. Is the stuff in this structure only related to alternate modes? If so, should it be called struct alt_mode_info?\n\nIt looks like \"discovery\" is not taken here. I am disinclined towards another abbreviation like \"ami.\"\n\nShould pd_dfp_pe_init be pd_dfp_discovery_init?",
      "parentUuid": "14473ef8_d1479373",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "6188f04e8e7b5eac7c38e948fab114b456d8d406",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5334455_53e080be",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 290,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-02T22:56:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the structure stores the information we collect to support alternate modes and only exists when we\u0027ve defined CONFIG_USB_PD_ALT_MODE_DFP.  I\u0027m honestly not certain why it was called policy to begin with, as it just stores and tracks the discovery process results plus info for modes we enter. We do have plans for an actual policy driver in the future though, which is why I\u0027d like to re-name now.\n\nDiscovery works.  Within functions, I\u0027m inclined to keep it to a very short name as the pointer is referenced a lot within things like for loops which become progressively less readable the longer the name gets.",
      "parentUuid": "8e11df6f_c0a28678",
